# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Values are inlined by react-native-config at BUILD time,
# so changing anything here means rebuilding the native app — Metro will not pick it up.
# Every key added here must also be declared in src/shared/env/react-native-config.d.ts.

CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sandbox build
#
# The sandbox flavor reads `.env.sandbox`, NOT `.env` — see `envConfigFiles` in
# android/app/build.gradle and ENVFILE in the iOS sandbox configuration. So a second
# file is needed, carrying at minimum:
#
#   OPES_ENV=sandbox
#
# `OPES_ENV=sandbox` is the ONLY value that turns the sandbox build on: an absent key,
# an empty string, `Sandbox`, or anything else all mean the normal build. Without that
# file the sandbox flavor still installs under its own bundle id — so it can never touch
# the real app's data — but it behaves like a normal build in every other way.
